    "text": "In the circuit shown in the figure,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>. The currents flowing through <math><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> are <math><msub><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> , respectively.<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/WhatsApp_Image_2020-07-01_at_11.33.58_AM.jpeg\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 142px;\" /><br />\r<br />\rImmediately after connecting switch <math><msub><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></math>,",
