  "solution": {
    "text": "At <math><mi>t</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn></math> , circuit can be considered as follows.<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/hhvdiszctupfmdnskaaydokznskyicyfpxtlkwvvegwtxmwphg.jpeg\" /><br /><br />After a long time, circuit can be considered as follows.<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/eftejvfempvmjxycrgwyxbpaemiocqrdebzbbiqctpfzhcvvga.jpeg\" /><br /><br />The current&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is zero at the instant of closing the switch but with time it grows and achieves a non-zero value, hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
